WEBVTT

00:01.376 --> 00:02.092
We are back.

00:02.092 --> 00:04.796
Welcome back!

00:05.839 --> 00:07.925
- We rode on Kaiser!
- We rode on Kaiser!

00:07.925 --> 00:09.051
- Kaiser?
- Kaiser?

00:09.051 --> 00:10.469
Ah, they meant...

00:10.469 --> 00:13.055
A fish let us to ride on its back.

00:14.264 --> 00:16.141
It's actually a Leviathan, though...

00:16.141 --> 00:18.018
Really, is that so?

00:18.018 --> 00:20.103
- It was really sparkly!
- It was really sparkly!

00:20.103 --> 00:21.146
Sparkly?

00:21.772 --> 00:25.275
Snow-like white flakes fluttered around us
in the middle of the way.

00:25.275 --> 00:26.735
It was very beautiful.

00:26.735 --> 00:30.405
Oh my, that's actually
quite a rare scenery!

00:30.405 --> 00:33.116
Indeed! You have a really good luck!

00:33.116 --> 00:34.368
Is that true?

00:34.952 --> 00:37.538
The sea is so beautiful.

00:37.538 --> 00:40.004
You must be tired from
all of that, right?

00:40.004 --> 00:42.459
Please take a good rest here.

00:42.459 --> 00:46.588
Well, it is hard to say this,
but we would like to excuse ourselves.

00:47.172 --> 00:50.175
Eh? You want to go back already?

00:50.175 --> 00:52.302
We still haven't given enough hospitality.

00:52.302 --> 00:55.764
No, no. It's more than enough already.

00:55.764 --> 00:58.784
Is that so? That's too bad.

00:58.786 --> 01:01.052
You have your own schedule,

01:01.052 --> 01:04.189
it would be selfish
to ask you to stay, right?

01:04.189 --> 01:07.192
I have an idea!
Would you wait a little bit?

01:09.736 --> 01:11.697
Please take this.

01:11.697 --> 01:13.365
What? The forbidden jewelled box?!

01:15.993 --> 01:18.579
Please enjoy it on your trip.

01:18.579 --> 01:20.414
Oh, it's a lunch box...

01:20.914 --> 01:22.291
Thank you very much.

01:23.128 --> 01:24.476
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

01:26.503 --> 01:28.423
Please visit us again!

01:28.424 --> 01:30.048
Be careful!

01:30.048 --> 01:31.862
Goodbye!

01:31.863 --> 01:33.051
Bye-bye!

01:33.051 --> 01:35.721
All right, let's go back on land!

01:35.721 --> 01:37.431
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

01:45.731 --> 01:51.021
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly familiarize ourselves♪

01:51.021 --> 01:56.072
(A Journey Through Another World:
Raising Kids While Adventuring)\

01:57.367 --> 02:02.247
♪The adventure to a new world is beginning♪

02:02.497 --> 02:07.085
♪Into a journey where
we can find fun things♪

02:09.087 --> 02:13.967
♪There are many encounters,
it's so exciting♪

02:13.967 --> 02:20.014
♪If you're with your family,
the things you can do will multiply♪

02:20.014 --> 02:23.006
♪It's okay to worry,
but you must not be overprotective♪

02:23.006 --> 02:26.021
♪I want you to praise me when
I try something and succeed♪

02:26.021 --> 02:28.815
♪It will be a wonderful party
if we can do this and that♪

02:28.815 --> 02:33.695
♪Because we will be together forever♪

02:34.237 --> 02:37.491
♪Please pat my head♪

02:37.491 --> 02:39.993
♪With your hand that I truly love♪

02:39.993 --> 02:45.916
♪I will send you thank you from
the deepest part of my heart, okay?♪

02:45.916 --> 02:48.627
♪Please pat me more♪

02:48.627 --> 02:51.755
♪See me with those eyes
filled with kindness♪

02:51.755 --> 02:58.095
♪I want this smile to last,
forever and ever♪

02:58.095 --> 03:03.767
♪Leisurely, leisurely,
let's slowly walk on♪

03:04.267 --> 03:09.648
♪Leisurely, Yururing,
I am happy, Travel Days♪

03:12.734 --> 03:16.738
(Crab! Crab!)

03:19.408 --> 03:21.118
- Oh, it's crabby!
- Oh, it's crabby!

03:24.538 --> 03:26.123
- We beat it!
- We beat it!

03:26.123 --> 03:27.749
- Ah!
- More is coming!

03:27.749 --> 03:29.584
Let's make crab hot pot today.

03:34.297 --> 03:35.424
What is this place?

03:41.847 --> 03:42.931
It's a labyrinth!

03:44.015 --> 03:45.642
It looks quite deep.

03:47.894 --> 03:50.772
- Yay!
- Wait! Hang on a minute!

04:02.492 --> 04:04.286
There's a teleportation device.

04:04.286 --> 04:05.704
This must be the starting point.

04:06.246 --> 04:07.789
Let's get out of the water.

04:09.001 --> 04:11.168
- Come, Alan.
- Yes.

04:11.168 --> 04:12.127
Heave-ho.

04:12.127 --> 04:13.628
Next, Elena.

04:19.676 --> 04:22.345
(5Зrd Labyrinth, "Ripple", 0/30 Floors)
Labyrinth number 53, "Ripple".

04:23.018 --> 04:26.433
So this is a mid-level labyrinth
with a total of 30 floors.

04:26.433 --> 04:29.978
There are teleportation devices
on every ten floors.

04:29.978 --> 04:31.613
Now, what should we do?

04:31.615 --> 04:32.758
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

04:32.076 --> 04:36.081
We can, but aren't you tired from
diving continuously by the sea?

04:36.812 --> 04:38.023
- We're fine!
- We're fine!

04:39.112 --> 04:40.155
Well then,

04:40.155 --> 04:44.367
let's go to the tenth floor and then
back to the city to rest a bit, okay?

04:44.367 --> 04:47.012
We can continue the rest another time.

04:47.012 --> 04:48.997
- Okay! We understand!
- Okay! We understand!

04:48.997 --> 04:52.959
Before that, it's about noon
so let's eat the lunch we got.

04:52.959 --> 04:55.837
- Yay! Meal!
- Yay! Meal!

04:57.839 --> 04:59.341
Looks yummy!

04:59.341 --> 05:01.384
- Let's dig in!
- Let's dig in!

05:02.677 --> 05:04.024
After lunch,

05:04.024 --> 05:04.262
("Ripple" Labyrinth, First Floor)
After lunch,

05:04.262 --> 05:08.091
("Ripple" Labyrinth, First Floor)
we went straight to explore
the first floor of the labyrinth.

05:08.934 --> 05:10.056
Where should we go?

05:10.056 --> 05:12.562
- Umm...
- Umm...

05:12.562 --> 05:13.563
- That way!
- That way!

05:13.563 --> 05:14.094
Okay! Left it is, then.

05:17.004 --> 05:19.027
Poison Frog, huh?

05:21.363 --> 05:24.491
These monsters have poison,
so use your magic, got it?

05:24.491 --> 05:25.575
- Okay!
- Okay!

05:26.076 --> 05:27.452
Air Shot!

05:30.497 --> 05:32.082
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

05:39.525 --> 05:42.862
Let's aim again.
You'll hit them in the next try.

05:42.864 --> 05:43.677
- Okay!
- Okay!

05:44.594 --> 05:46.388
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

05:48.431 --> 05:50.225
- We got it!
- We got it!

05:50.225 --> 05:51.935
Whoa, you did it!

05:54.229 --> 05:58.004
("Ripple" Labyrinth, Second Floor)

06:00.061 --> 06:02.487
- Ah, this wall...
- Ah, this wall...

06:02.487 --> 06:04.406
Yeah. This looks suspicious.

06:04.099 --> 06:05.991
Appraise.

06:07.113 --> 06:08.823
Good, there is no trap.

06:13.054 --> 06:15.333
So it is a hidden room.

06:15.333 --> 06:16.585
- Yay!
- Yay!

06:18.128 --> 06:20.297
- Treasure chest!
- Can we open?

06:20.297 --> 06:21.798
Yes, you can.

06:23.624 --> 06:25.042
What is this?

06:25.044 --> 06:26.097
These are called red prawns.

06:26.097 --> 06:28.352
Is it good?

06:28.353 --> 06:29.089
Yeah, maybe.

06:29.089 --> 06:31.141
- Can we eat it?
- Can we eat it?

06:31.141 --> 06:32.934
Now? Raw?

06:34.247 --> 06:38.189
I will cook it later for you,
so let's set it aside for now.

06:38.189 --> 06:39.357
- Okay!
- Okay!

06:40.317 --> 06:42.319
- There's a treasure chest over there too!
- There's a treasure chest over there too!

06:44.798 --> 06:46.899
- What is this?
- A tree?

06:48.825 --> 06:50.201
A dried bonito?

06:50.201 --> 06:53.288
This is a dried fish.

06:53.288 --> 06:54.581
- Is it food?
- Is it food?

06:54.581 --> 06:57.005
You can't eat it just as is,

06:57.005 --> 06:59.502
but it is tasty
if we use it in cooking.

07:01.254 --> 07:04.591
I'm surprised, but this is delightful.

07:05.258 --> 07:07.552
Now I can cook meals
that need this in their broth!

07:08.261 --> 07:10.597
Let's open more treasure chests!

07:10.597 --> 07:12.307
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

07:13.126 --> 07:14.267
White prawns!

07:15.107 --> 07:16.102
Asari clams!

07:16.102 --> 07:18.563
Kelp... Seaweed?

07:18.563 --> 07:20.732
There is nothing but seafood here!

07:20.732 --> 07:22.525
(Big Catch)
This labyrinth is surprising!

07:22.525 --> 07:24.903
Well, I'm happy to get them, though.

07:27.989 --> 07:30.283
These stairs will take us
to the sixth floor.

07:30.951 --> 07:32.452
But it's late already.

07:32.452 --> 07:35.083
Let's call it a day
and have dinner here today.

07:35.083 --> 07:37.165
- Okay!
- Okay!

07:38.208 --> 07:40.126
What to have for today?

07:40.071 --> 07:43.046
Oh, right! We have some Sand Crabs.

07:43.038 --> 07:47.509
Let's use the dried bonito that we got
as a broth, and make a crab hot pot!

07:47.717 --> 07:51.054
- Crab! Crab! Crab!
- Crab! Crab! Crab!

07:55.934 --> 07:57.894
- It's delicious!
- It's delicious!

07:58.436 --> 08:00.772
- Big Bro!
- We want more crab!

08:00.772 --> 08:01.856
Yes, sure!

08:02.399 --> 08:05.819
I tried boiling the red
and white prawns in salt...

08:10.074 --> 08:12.534
It's so puffy!

08:12.534 --> 08:14.661
- Puffy!
- Puffy!

08:15.037 --> 08:17.622
This is quite a great labyrinth.

08:21.871 --> 08:23.586
And the next morning,

08:23.586 --> 08:26.297
("Ripple" Labyrinth, Sixth Floor)
we began exploring from the sixth floor.

08:26.776 --> 08:28.056
You're no longer tired, right?

08:28.562 --> 08:29.551
- Not at all!
- Not at all!

08:30.051 --> 08:32.053
Oh, a big clam!

08:32.053 --> 08:33.513
It's an Impact Shell.

08:34.222 --> 08:35.724
Hold it!

08:35.724 --> 08:39.644
If we hit them,
it will emit a shockwave.

08:39.644 --> 08:42.023
So we must attack from a distance.

08:42.023 --> 08:44.107
- Okay!
- Okay!

08:44.107 --> 08:47.068
- Slowly, quietly...
- Slowly, quietly...

08:47.068 --> 08:48.082
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

08:52.049 --> 08:54.117
Yes, well done!

08:56.453 --> 08:59.789
Oh right, I haven't checked
their status for a while.

09:01.013 --> 09:02.097
(Alan, Job: Boxer, Level 25)
(Skills: Water Magic, Hand-to-Hand Combat)

09:02.979 --> 09:05.398
They're now the Children of the God of Water.

09:05.004 --> 09:08.011
Is it because I know their identity,

09:08.011 --> 09:08.131
(Title: Children of the God of Water)

09:08.131 --> 09:12.007
(Title: Children of the God of Water)
or is it because my Appraise skill leveled up?

09:12.093 --> 09:16.556
Elena is the same. Level 25.

09:17.432 --> 09:19.517
Wait, this is bad.

09:19.079 --> 09:20.185
- What is this? - I don't know.

09:20.185 --> 09:21.087
- I am level 27.
- What is this?  - I don't know.

09:21.096 --> 09:22.145
- I am level 27.
- I wonder...  - Yeah...

09:22.145 --> 09:23.035
- Our levels are not so far apart.
- I wonder...  - Yeah...

09:24.189 --> 09:27.358
I'll look pathetic if they overtake me.

09:27.358 --> 09:28.693
Big Bro!

09:29.431 --> 09:31.154
We picked this up.

09:31.154 --> 09:32.549
Thank you.

09:32.055 --> 09:34.199
Huh, a party popper?

09:34.199 --> 09:36.618
Another odd item came up.

09:36.618 --> 09:38.244
What is that?

09:38.244 --> 09:39.829
This is a party popper.

09:39.829 --> 09:42.969
If we pull the string here,
it will make a loud sound.

09:42.971 --> 09:44.209
Do you want to try it?

09:44.209 --> 09:45.293
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

09:45.293 --> 09:50.715
Then make sure the blunt end is not
pointing at anyone, then pull its string.

09:50.715 --> 09:51.913
- Okay!
- Okay!

09:57.263 --> 10:01.142
Wh-What the heck?
That was too loud.

10:02.006 --> 10:05.023
Sorry. That must have shocked you.

10:05.023 --> 10:06.773
Sorry, sorry.

10:09.734 --> 10:11.694
Oh, Impact shell.

10:11.694 --> 10:13.404
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

10:22.455 --> 10:25.542
Are they okay?
Were they traumatized?

10:25.542 --> 10:29.629
Let's take it anyway because
this may be useful for something.

10:30.069 --> 10:31.464
("Ripple" Labyrinth, Tenth Floor)

10:31.464 --> 10:35.051
("Ripple" Labyrinth, Tenth Floor)
After that, we arrived at the tenth floor.

10:35.844 --> 10:37.303
In a mid-level labyrinth,

10:37.303 --> 10:39.597
there's a sub-boss room
on every ten floors.

10:40.064 --> 10:41.007
This is the room.

10:41.702 --> 10:44.076
Are you ready?
Be on your guard, okay?

10:44.762 --> 10:45.895
- Okay!
- Okay!

10:52.694 --> 10:54.529
So much water!

11:01.087 --> 11:03.083
Wait, wait up!

11:04.717 --> 11:06.427
Let's walk slowly, okay?

11:08.334 --> 11:09.919
There's a monster here.

11:11.857 --> 11:13.423
That's an Arrowfish.

11:13.425 --> 11:14.591
Wind Cutter!

11:16.005 --> 11:17.552
Wind Cutter!

11:17.594 --> 11:19.679
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

11:19.679 --> 11:20.889
Wind Cutter!

11:20.889 --> 11:22.473
- Water Ball!
- Water Ball!

11:22.473 --> 11:25.476
- Wind Cutter! Wind Cutter!
- Water Ball! Water Ball!

11:28.938 --> 11:31.009
We defeated like a hundred of them...

11:31.009 --> 11:33.651
- The presence is gone!
- The presence is gone!

11:33.651 --> 11:36.362
Yeah, it looks like it's over.

11:38.528 --> 11:40.028
So the exit gate is over there...

11:40.282 --> 11:42.243
Big Bro! Look!

11:42.243 --> 11:43.328
So many!

11:43.328 --> 11:46.122
Wow, there really are a lot!

11:46.122 --> 11:50.668
Fairy stones, Arrowfish fillet...
Also some arrows and spears.

11:50.668 --> 11:52.003
Thank you, both of you.

11:52.003 --> 11:53.213
There, there.

11:53.796 --> 11:56.341
Okay! Let's go to that cliff.

11:57.858 --> 11:58.817
Huh?

11:59.427 --> 12:01.471
Big Bro, below us.

12:01.471 --> 12:03.014
Something is there.

12:03.014 --> 12:05.434
Eh? Below, like underwater?

12:05.436 --> 12:06.354
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

12:06.356 --> 12:07.281
Detect.

12:08.269 --> 12:10.021
There's no monster around.

12:10.021 --> 12:12.608
It seems safe. Want to dive in?

12:12.061 --> 12:14.025
- Yeah, let's go!
- Yeah, let's go!

12:19.205 --> 12:20.448
There it is!

12:20.448 --> 12:22.367
A huge treasure chest!

12:22.367 --> 12:24.285
Good job finding it!

12:27.058 --> 12:28.957
- We have the same ones!
- We have the same ones!

12:28.957 --> 12:30.833
Yeah, it's the mermaid bracelet.

12:31.417 --> 12:34.796
I wonder if this is a rare item
since we found it on this floor.

12:35.505 --> 12:39.425
Well, we can equip the spares
for Joule and the others.

12:40.051 --> 12:42.637
And it doesn't seem like
there is anything else.

12:52.023 --> 12:54.107
Oh, a teleportation device.

12:54.857 --> 12:57.318
Let's end the labyrinth exploration here.

12:57.318 --> 13:00.446
Let's go back to the first floor,
then go to Bailey City tomorrow.

13:00.446 --> 13:02.407
- City?
- Let's go!

13:02.407 --> 13:03.533
Okay.

13:11.499 --> 13:13.001
We have arrived!

13:14.137 --> 13:16.296
This is Bailey City.

13:16.296 --> 13:17.088
Bailey!

13:17.088 --> 13:22.302
We have Sir Risner's introduction letter
for the provincial lord, but...

13:22.802 --> 13:25.763
Now let's drop by after
we look around the city for a bit.

13:25.763 --> 13:26.723
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

13:28.308 --> 13:29.892
Delicious smell!

13:29.892 --> 13:31.269
I know, right?

13:31.269 --> 13:34.048
Oh, it's scallop.
Those are huge!

13:34.048 --> 13:35.481
Welcome!

13:35.481 --> 13:38.943
We just fished it this morning.
Won't you try some?

13:38.943 --> 13:41.321
Is this seasoned with salt?

13:41.321 --> 13:42.655
Yes, that's right.

13:44.324 --> 13:46.826
Salt is good, but in the end...

13:46.826 --> 13:50.121
Excuse me, if I may,
I want to season it myself.

13:50.121 --> 13:52.415
Oh? I don't mind that.

13:52.415 --> 13:54.834
- Then, give me three.
- Gotcha!

13:54.834 --> 13:56.753
Please excuse me.

14:09.849 --> 14:11.726
It's still hot, so be careful.

14:11.726 --> 14:12.081
- Yes!
- Yes!

14:18.702 --> 14:20.635
How is it? Good?

14:20.637 --> 14:22.431
- Great!
- Great!

14:24.947 --> 14:27.827
Yep! Butter and soy sauce
is indeed the way to go!

14:27.829 --> 14:29.654
That looks good, Young Man.

14:30.087 --> 14:35.083
I know butter, but was that
black liquid you added next?

14:36.584 --> 14:40.797
That's the sap of the Kokuichi tree.
It's a seasoning called soy sauce.

14:40.797 --> 14:43.383
- Would you like to try it?
- Can I?!

14:47.218 --> 14:49.303
So good!

14:49.305 --> 14:52.266
What's this?
It's a taste I never had before.

14:52.266 --> 14:53.559
So darn good!

14:53.559 --> 14:56.104
Old man, that looks good!
Let me try, too!

14:56.104 --> 14:58.439
- Me too!
- I want that too!

14:59.357 --> 15:00.691
So many people are coming...

15:00.691 --> 15:02.652
- I won't give any!
- I won't give any!

15:03.082 --> 15:06.114
It's all right.
No one will take yours.

15:06.114 --> 15:10.243
Sorry, Young Man!
But would you sell that soy sauce?

15:10.243 --> 15:13.788
Sure, I don't mind.
I'm responsible for this anyway.

15:13.788 --> 15:17.166
And could you also pass
some of the butter, too?

15:17.166 --> 15:18.793
Ah, sure thing.

15:20.837 --> 15:22.063
So good!

15:23.084 --> 15:26.003
- It's delicious!
- So yummy!

15:26.342 --> 15:28.261
I want it too!

15:29.637 --> 15:31.139
Sorry, it's sold out!

15:31.139 --> 15:32.723
What?!

15:35.091 --> 15:39.512
I have never sold out this fast,
not since the first day I opened the shop.

15:39.514 --> 15:41.349
That was a large crowd.

15:41.351 --> 15:44.358
That seasoning does not exist
around here after all.

15:44.036 --> 15:47.266
I got carried away and sold it,

15:47.268 --> 15:50.062
but can I sell it with
that seasoning from now on?

15:50.064 --> 15:52.076
Yes, I don't mind.

15:52.743 --> 15:55.955
But you have to procure
the soy sauce yourself.

15:55.955 --> 15:58.439
Why, of course! Thank you!

15:58.441 --> 16:00.042
It's set now!

16:00.918 --> 16:04.672
I will go find soy sauce immediately!

16:04.672 --> 16:06.799
See you, Young Man!

16:06.799 --> 16:08.176
Wait, what about your shop?!

16:08.176 --> 16:10.136
- He's gone.
- He's gone.

16:10.136 --> 16:11.637
There he goes.

16:11.637 --> 16:14.765
Big Bro, where are we going next?

16:14.765 --> 16:16.267
Let's see...

16:16.851 --> 16:18.728
Here we are! A blacksmith!

16:20.064 --> 16:21.084
Excuse me!

16:22.356 --> 16:23.774
Oh, what is it?

16:23.774 --> 16:26.986
I want you to polish this.

16:26.986 --> 16:31.437
Kaiser told us to carry it around,
but it's too big.

16:31.439 --> 16:33.091
This is not a rock, but a scale?

16:34.264 --> 16:36.037
It's super hard and thick.

16:37.788 --> 16:40.416
This mana... It's impossible!

16:40.416 --> 16:43.377
This is not something
you just pick up randomly!

16:43.377 --> 16:45.463
Well, it sure is not.

16:45.463 --> 16:46.881
He's sharp.

16:46.881 --> 16:48.299
It's a present, Sir.

16:48.301 --> 16:51.304
Just who the hell is giving
this important item?

16:51.886 --> 16:53.346
I can't tell you!

16:53.888 --> 16:56.516
Well, of course,
for something like this...

16:56.516 --> 16:58.643
Then what to do after polishing?

16:58.643 --> 17:00.311
We want it to be easy to carry.

17:00.311 --> 17:03.064
Can you make some kind of hole
so we can put a string through?

17:04.695 --> 17:08.000
A hole is not possible
because it will surely break.

17:08.861 --> 17:10.279
What should I do...

17:10.279 --> 17:12.099
Hey, Rudy! Come here!

17:12.099 --> 17:14.575
Yes, what is it?

17:14.575 --> 17:17.247
Can you turn this into an accessory?

17:17.249 --> 17:19.016
What? A rock?

17:19.789 --> 17:21.791
It's a shard of a water dragon scale.

17:21.791 --> 17:23.543
What?! Seriously?!

17:24.293 --> 17:26.879
You're good at this kind of craft, right?

17:26.879 --> 17:28.339
Well, yeah...

17:28.339 --> 17:30.883
Can you turn it into a pendant?

17:30.883 --> 17:32.009
Ah...

17:32.677 --> 17:34.047
Please wait.

17:35.429 --> 17:40.309
Let's make it this shape...
But it'd be too weak...

17:40.309 --> 17:43.854
Then, change it like this...
Then like this!

17:44.105 --> 17:45.731
Done!

17:45.731 --> 17:47.009
What about this?

17:47.009 --> 17:49.694
Oh, that's splendid!

17:49.694 --> 17:52.028
- So cool!
- Beautiful!

17:52.028 --> 17:54.049
Then can we order that?

17:54.049 --> 17:55.007
Sure.

17:55.007 --> 17:59.062
But using copper and silver as the frame
won't look good with the scale,

17:59.062 --> 18:02.582
so we need a better material.

18:02.582 --> 18:06.054
But that will hike up the price...

18:06.056 --> 18:07.962
Can you give an example?

18:08.713 --> 18:10.423
I guess...

18:10.423 --> 18:12.174
Something like mythril...

18:13.134 --> 18:15.261
That's such a fantasy stuff!

18:15.261 --> 18:17.138
Do you have the materials?

18:17.138 --> 18:19.724
Do you have to procure it?

18:19.724 --> 18:23.003
Boss, we have some mythril, right?

18:23.032 --> 18:25.104
Can we use it?

18:25.104 --> 18:27.481
- Yeah, I don't mind.
- All right!

18:27.481 --> 18:31.444
Can you make the chain part
something like a leather string?

18:31.444 --> 18:34.947
Yes, but a common leather
won't be a good material.

18:36.616 --> 18:39.041
I guess as an artisan,
he has a quirk he wants to uphold.

18:39.041 --> 18:43.497
Mythril spider's thread will be ideal.

18:43.497 --> 18:46.626
Don't be stupid.
No way anyone can get that.

18:46.626 --> 18:48.127
You're right...

18:48.127 --> 18:50.671
Mythril Spider?

18:50.671 --> 18:54.091
I think something like that
was among what Syl gave me.

18:54.592 --> 18:56.052
Is this much enough?

19:00.473 --> 19:02.683
How could you have it?!

19:02.683 --> 19:04.056
That's loud, what's wrong?

19:09.312 --> 19:12.044
You, I can't believe
you are carrying that around.

19:14.195 --> 19:16.989
So this material is that astonishing?

19:16.989 --> 19:19.659
I want three of the pendants.

19:19.659 --> 19:22.787
- Three?
- Yes, for these kids, too.

19:22.787 --> 19:25.581
For the kids? Such a luxury.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.334
It's a charm.

19:28.334 --> 19:31.504
So that we may get the Water's Blessing.

19:31.504 --> 19:33.013
I just made that up.

19:33.013 --> 19:34.084
I see.

19:34.084 --> 19:37.927
It's a rare chance to work
with rare materials like these,

19:37.927 --> 19:39.512
so I'm very grateful.

19:39.512 --> 19:46.018
Then, instead of three similar ones,
why don't we vary the designs?

19:46.018 --> 19:47.478
Please, that'd be great!

19:47.478 --> 19:49.772
What design do you want?

19:49.772 --> 19:50.094
A cute one!

19:50.094 --> 19:52.316
And Alan?

19:54.168 --> 19:56.422
- Just leave it to him?
- Yes!

19:56.862 --> 19:59.824
Usually they gave the same answer,

19:59.824 --> 20:02.243
but in times like this,
their characters show.

20:02.243 --> 20:05.545
Then I'll begin working right away!

20:05.547 --> 20:07.385
Please, thank you.

20:07.387 --> 20:08.582
Oh, I just remember.

20:08.582 --> 20:12.962
Can we also request equipment
if we have the materials?

20:12.962 --> 20:15.506
Of course. What are the materials?

20:15.506 --> 20:16.006
It's these.

20:16.006 --> 20:17.174
(Evil Viper's Skin)
It's these.

20:17.174 --> 20:18.023
(Evil Viper's Skin)

20:20.072 --> 20:22.014
Oh, shut up, Boss.

20:26.565 --> 20:28.058
I see.

20:28.006 --> 20:31.522
So you're an A-rank adventurer.

20:31.522 --> 20:36.902
I thought I was a good judge after seeing
many adventurers for a long time...

20:37.611 --> 20:40.197
But you can't judge by looks alone.

20:41.991 --> 20:45.244
Guild master Shireen
said the same thing.

20:45.244 --> 20:47.204
So, what do you want to make?

20:47.204 --> 20:50.249
Gloves for harvesting,
a breastplate, and a bracer.

20:50.249 --> 20:52.877
Bracer? Not from metal
but from leather?

20:52.877 --> 20:55.004
Yes. We have a hawk as a pet.

20:55.004 --> 20:58.716
When he lands on my arm,
his talons kind of stab...

20:58.716 --> 21:00.342
I got it.

21:02.018 --> 21:03.866
What is it, Alan?

21:03.868 --> 21:05.389
I want one too.

21:05.389 --> 21:07.391
What? A glove?

21:07.391 --> 21:09.225
No. For Bolt.

21:09.227 --> 21:11.813
Do you want Bolt to land
on your arm, too?

21:11.815 --> 21:12.073
Yes!

21:12.073 --> 21:14.106
I see. Okay, then.

21:14.693 --> 21:16.069
Let's make one for you too.

21:16.071 --> 21:18.068
Really? Yay!

21:18.812 --> 21:24.985
Since Elena said she did not need it,
we asked for two and left the store.

21:25.751 --> 21:27.087
I can't wait for it to finish.

21:27.087 --> 21:29.747
- Yes, I can't wait!
- Yes, I can't wait!

21:29.747 --> 21:32.075
And now, it's time to visit Syl.

21:35.091 --> 21:36.629
Syl, are you there?

21:39.853 --> 21:41.091
Takumi!

21:41.091 --> 21:44.053
It's been a while! You seem well.

21:44.053 --> 21:47.223
Thankfully.
We arrived safely in Bailey.

21:47.223 --> 21:50.768
Also, I have heard about
Alan and Elena...

21:50.768 --> 21:53.479
...that they are the Children
of the God of Water.

21:53.479 --> 21:55.773
I am sorry for not telling you.

21:55.773 --> 21:58.275
Nah, you have no need to apologize.

21:58.275 --> 22:00.627
But, can I ask something?

22:00.628 --> 22:01.695
Yes?

22:01.695 --> 22:05.908
Where and what their father
is doing right now?

22:10.746 --> 22:12.289
Yay!

22:12.289 --> 22:13.499
Wait up!

22:28.472 --> 22:32.434
♪Forever, all the time♪

22:32.434 --> 22:35.604
♪I just can't keep crying♪

22:35.604 --> 22:36.647
♪Ah! Ah!♪

22:36.647 --> 22:40.276
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

22:40.276 --> 22:42.903
♪If I am with you♪

22:45.155 --> 22:47.199
♪Such a good weather♪

22:47.199 --> 22:50.786
♪Today, let's go slowly♪

22:50.786 --> 22:53.038
♪While taking detours♪

22:53.038 --> 22:57.585
♪The clear sky,
the wind caressing my cheeks♪

22:57.585 --> 23:00.838
♪And your gentle gaze♪

23:00.838 --> 23:04.091
♪Beyond an unknown road♪

23:04.091 --> 23:06.135
♪The wind blows past♪

23:06.135 --> 23:09.138
♪The curtain of light sways♪

23:09.889 --> 23:13.517
♪Maybe we should try going
I just feel like it♪

23:13.517 --> 23:20.024
♪No matter what happens
we can laugh anyway♪

23:22.234 --> 23:26.238
♪Forever, all the time♪

23:26.488 --> 23:29.241
♪I just can't keep crying♪

23:29.241 --> 23:30.492
♪Ah! Ah!♪

23:30.492 --> 23:33.996
♪In happy moments and sad moments♪

23:33.996 --> 23:37.166
♪If I am with you♪

23:38.334 --> 23:43.013
♪I am sure I'll be content♪

23:44.009 --> 23:45.941
(Next Episode)

23:45.941 --> 23:48.032
- What does...
- Papa mean?

23:48.032 --> 23:50.039
(Next Episode)
(What Does Papa Mean?)
